<article class="env-lemma" id="06EI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06EI">Lemma <span data-tag="06EI">67.25.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. If $f$ is locally of finite type, then $f(X_{\text{ft-pts}}) \subset Y_{\text{ft-pts}}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Take $x \in X_{\text{ft-pts}}$. Represent $x$ by a locally finite type morphism $x : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to X$. Then $f \circ x$ is locally of finite type by Lemma <a href="/tag/03XG" data-tag="03XG">67.23.2</a>. Hence $f(x) \in Y_{\text{ft-pts}}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>